        "declaration": "Matrix.PosSemidef.re_trace_finKronecker_mul_cfc_surprisal",
        "name_status": "declared"
      },
      "paper_sources": [
        {
          "version": "September 24, 2026",
          "path": "preprints/A-two-dimensional-area-law-from-a-global-spectral-gap-September-24-2026/build/sections/07-comparators.tex",
          "labels": [
            "comparator:high-label"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "license": "Apache-2.0",
      "notices": [],
      "changes": [
        "Independently derive the actual finite tensor-power spectral trace law and independent-copy Chebyshev concentration from the canonical eigenvalue distribution. Product logarithms are expanded only on nonzero product weights; no full-rank or supplied eigenbasis hypothesis is used. For PSD trace-one density matrices, the actual CFC threshold mass is at most k times the one-copy variance divided by w squared, and at width k^(3/4) the bound is the variance divided by sqrt k. The first three results allow k = 0; the simplified rate requires k > 0. Schur label selection and physical ground-state concentration are separate."
      ],
      "no_upstream_proof_text_reused": true,
      "verification": {
        "result": "passed",
